{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790541724,"nonce":"p7t8DX9Y+mctEyjannJq91IYu90=","message":"Step 4, decided, as Ash does it:\n- The runtime object carries ash_wasm_runtime::guest, adapted to the krio-fiber calls the fiber code makes. Every wasm AOT program imports env.ash_host_fiber_yield, ash_host_fiber_state and ash_host_fiber_arm, so it needs a host.\n- wlift run program.wasm is that host, built on ash_wasm_runtime's native host (Program::load / run), which also answers the socket, dlopen/dlsym and process imports. It replaces plain wasmtime program.wasm in the docs, as ash run does for Ash.\n- The unwind/rewind transform is a build flag, as ASH_WASM_FIBERS is for Ash: wlift --aot ... --aot-fibers links with LinkOptions::fibers. With it, Fiber.yield in compiled code suspends and resumes. Without it, the link is unchanged and a yield in compiled code raises as it does today.\n- The collector scans each suspended fiber's side stack and shadow stack, from the same place krio fibers' stacks are enumerated natively.","files":null}]}